From ed501d1c20a4308648d31a4888a3413f3dbed516 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:11:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] book ch.10: replication, power and equivalence (TOST)

- power_t (non-central t, one- and two-sided), replication_table for CRD,
  RCBD and Latin square (SED, LSD, power by n), sigma_from_range,
  split_plot_power with Satterthwaite df (Example 10.2).
- replication_power: plan replication from pilot data (ResMS, %CV, LSD as a
  fraction of the mean) or a given s2; minimal n for LSD <= delta and for
  target power.
- equivalence_test: TOST of each treatment (or factor combination) against a
  standard, absolute or percent margin, 100(1-2a)% intervals, equivalence and
  inequivalence decisions, optional Bonferroni, power for delta = c.
- Catalog, bridge, i18n and messages.
- Tests against Tables 10.1, 10.3, 10.4, 10.6, 10.7 and Examples 10.1A-C, 10.3.

